  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the given circuit &#39;a&#39; is an arbitrary constant. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> for which the equivalent circuit resistance is minimum, will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _____ .</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/a314768d-5e9a-466b-8a39-476d281a5a7d-image.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 163px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/7ef73449-292e-4f29-8438-cf6e70ef18d4-image.png\" style=\"width: 264px; height: 160px;\" /></p><p>Left part of the resistors are connected in parallel, hence&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Similarly, for the right part of the resistors we can write,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Therefore, equivalent resistance will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Differentiating both sides w.r.t&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;to observe critical points, we get&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>Thus,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
